meta {
  name: Refund Order
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/refund
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "amount": 5000,
    "paymentMode": "CASH"
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Refund part of an order's paid amount **without** cancelling it (the standalone
  "Refund Without Cancellation" action). Writes a REFUND row to the payment ledger
  and recomputes `paymentStatus` **and** `refundStatus` off the new effective paid
  amount. Works on active **and** already-cancelled orders (use it to top up a
  partial refund made at cancellation time).

  Body:
  - `amount` (minor units, required, ≥1) — returned to the patient.
  - `refundCharge` (minor units, default 0) — fee the lab retains out of the refund.
  - `paymentMode` (required) — `CASH | CREDIT | UPI | CARD | WALLET | BANK_TRANSFER`.
  - `reference?`, `paymentDate?` (ISO) — optional.

  `amount + refundCharge` is capped at the order's current **refundable balance**
  (`paid − cancellationCharge − refunds already made`):
  - exceeds it ⇒ 422 `REFUND_EXCEEDS_REFUNDABLE`
  - nothing left to refund ⇒ 422 `NOTHING_TO_REFUND`

  Gated by the branch's Registration Settings → Cancellation & Refund:
  - `AllowRefund` off ⇒ 422 `REFUND_NOT_ALLOWED`.
  - `RefundChargesApplicable` off ⇒ any `refundCharge` in the body is ignored
    (forced to 0); on ⇒ used, or defaults to the configured `RefundChargesAmount`.
  - `AllowPartialRefund` off ⇒ `amount` must equal the full refundable-to-patient
    (`refundable − refundCharge`), else 422 `PARTIAL_REFUND_NOT_ALLOWED`.

  The refunded total surfaces in the billing list's `refundedAmount`
  ("Refund Provided" column). The order's `refundStatus`
  (`NONE | PARTIALLY_REFUNDED | FULLY_REFUNDED`) is also updated, so the billing /
  refund lists fold the refund state into the Status label ("Refunded" /
  "Partially Refunded") instead of showing "Not Paid".
}
